+# DevPulse fork of kyutai-labs/moshi
+
+**Upstream:** https://github.com/kyutai-labs/moshi
+**Forked from:** main @ 6d14a619 (2026-04-24) — workspace.package.version 0.6.4
+**Fork version:** 0.6.5+devpulse
+**Reason for fork:** lift candle pins from 0.9.1 → 0.10 so the DevPulse Platform
+workspace ships a single candle version. Upstream Kyutai has not bumped to
+candle 0.10 (no PR, no tracking issue as of the fork date). Cadence pattern
+suggests mid-May 2026 if Kyutai keeps their ~6-week lag behind candle releases.
+
+## Why this fork exists, not a one-off branch
+
+The DevPulse workspace runs candle 0.10 across model-loader, mistral.rs, and
+all custom backends. Letting Cargo resolve a separate candle 0.9 transitively
+for moshi would compile two candle copies (~30 MB binary, ~2 min build).
+Pre-release rule (CLAUDE.md, project memory `feedback_no_backcompat_questions`):
+no shims, no dual-version backwards-compat. The fork is the clean path.
+
+## What changed
+
+Single-file patch in `rust/Cargo.toml`:
+
+```diff
+ [workspace.package]
+-version = "0.6.4"
++version = "0.6.5+devpulse"
+ description = "moshi, a real-time voice AI"
++description = "moshi, a real-time voice AI (devpulse fork)"
+```
+
+```diff
+ [workspace.dependencies]
+-candle = { version = "0.9.1",  package = "candle-core" }
+-candle-flash-attn = "0.9.1"
+-candle-nn = "0.9.1"
+-candle-transformers = "0.9.1"
++candle = { version = "0.10", package = "candle-core" }
++candle-flash-attn = "0.10"
++candle-nn = "0.10"
++candle-transformers = "0.10"
+```
+
+```diff
+ [workspace.dependencies]
+-moshi = { path = "./moshi-core", version = "0.6.4" }
++moshi = { path = "./moshi-core", version = "0.6.5+devpulse" }
+```
+
+**No source files were edited.** Audit run on 2026-04-26:
+
+- `grep -rn "match.*DType" rust/moshi-core/` → 0 hits. PR
+  [huggingface/candle#3412](https://github.com/huggingface/candle/pull/3412)
+  added `#[non_exhaustive]` to `DType` in candle 0.10. moshi-core uses `DType`
+  only as variants (`DType::F32`, `DType::BF16`) and as a type, never in an
+  exhaustive `match`. No source change needed.
+- `grep -rn "UgIOp1\|Error::Ug\|::compile(" rust/moshi-core/` → 0 hits. PR
+  [huggingface/candle#3268](https://github.com/huggingface/candle/pull/3268)
+  gated `ug` behind a feature flag. moshi-core does not call into it.
+  No source change needed.
+
+If a future candle 0.10.x patch breaks moshi-core's actual surface (`Tensor`,
+`candle-nn` layers, `quantized_var_builder`, `WithDType::to_cpu_storage_owned`),
+patch *here* and append the change to this file with the cargo error and the
+chosen fix.
+
+## How to re-sync to upstream
+
+When Kyutai ships a candle-0.10-compatible release upstream (target signal:
+`rust/Cargo.toml` on `main` shows `candle = "0.10"`):
+
+```bash
+cd deps/moshi
+git fetch origin
+git checkout origin/main         # or the new release tag
+# Confirm rust/Cargo.toml workspace pins are 0.10
+# Drop deps/moshi/PATCHES.md (this file)
+# Drop the moshi entry from the platform workspace [patch.crates-io]
+# Switch model-loader Cargo.toml back to crates.io: moshi = "0.7" (or whatever upstream ships)
+cargo update -p moshi
+cargo check -p model-loader --features moshi-sts,cuda
+```
+
+If `cargo check` is green after that sequence, delete this fork — `deps/moshi/`
+goes away, the `[patch.crates-io]` entry goes away, and we're back on the
+published crate.
+
+## Workspace coupling
+
+The fork is wired into the platform workspace via:
+
+- `Cargo.toml` (root) — `[patch.crates-io]` entry pointing `moshi` at
+  `deps/moshi/rust/moshi-core`.
+- `kernel/model-loader/Cargo.toml` — depends on `moshi = "0.6"` with
+  `default-features = false` (no flash-attn). The patch re-targets this to
+  the local path; the version range `^0.6` is satisfied by `0.6.5+devpulse`.
+
+Sibling crates inside `deps/moshi/rust/` (mimi-pyo3, moshi-cli, moshi-server,
+moshi-backend) are *not* compiled by the platform workspace. Cargo only
+resolves the patched `moshi` crate. The sibling Cargo.tomls stay untouched.
